WEBVTT

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.240
Yakumo...

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.110
...Sumeragi?

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.840
Karen.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:58.890
You really assumed
Yakumo Sumeragi's identity?

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:03.270
What is this?

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:39.280
"Slumbering Desire"

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:43.740
It was never like this... before.

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.040
Karen.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:51.250
You've been here for 2,000 years?

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:52.750
I don't understand.

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:57.340
Karen, there's something
we need your help with.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:01.890
Please help us destroy the Kunad Gate.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:06.810
You used Arahabaki

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:10.190
and the Red Strings
to travel through time.

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:14.060
And when you interacted
with events 2,000 years ago,

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.940
it created an entanglement.

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:20.530
As long as it persists,
the Kunad Gate won't disappear.

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:22.240
That's right.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:25.450
The world will be destroyed
unless we do something.

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:27.290
That's why you have to--

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.540
It won't solve anything.

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:31.290
What?

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:35.840
The one who creates an entanglement
is the one who can unravel it.

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:38.630
We know because we've done it ourselves.

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:40.130
I know that.

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:41.760
You do?

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.800
Then why won't you help?

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:45.970
It won't solve anything.

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:48.350
That is a fact.

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:52.940
What do you mean?

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:58.820
Karen! You traveled through time
to save Alice, didn't you?

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:01.990
So then why go back 2,000 years?

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:05.910
I didn't understand... at first.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:07.330
At first?

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:13.290
You know that Yakumo Sumeragi
was a Red Strings user.

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:17.960
I believe I was drawn to that power.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:20.590
Back 2,000 years without any thought?

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:23.010
I was searching.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:26.800
Searching for a way to
save Alice 2,000 years later.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:29.510
A way to change the future.

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:34.230
Your solution was to assume
Yakumo Sumeragi's identity?

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:36.230
I was certain I could do something

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:39.900
if I used the office of
our nation's founder.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:43.070
Do something? What could you do?

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:49.740
Ages after that time,
I found the only way to save Alice.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:52.790
The only way?

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:57.250
I connected myself to Arahabaki.

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:10.060
I thought if I connected with Arahabaki,
the heart of all other systems,

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:14.810
I could save Alice by changing history.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:17.350
Now this is interesting.

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:21.860
A bio computer in which Arahabaki
incorporates your brain?

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:26.860
So those intrusions into
our brains were your doing?

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:28.740
I don't understand.

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:32.580
After all that,
why hasn't Alice come back?

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:36.250
That is why I've tried over and over.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.040
Over and over?

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.210
Countless iterations of myself

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:47.180
have traveled through time
to take Yakumo's place.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:48.640
What do you mean?!

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:52.060
Dimension entanglements occur each time.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:56.140
But if I try to unravel them,
I can't bring Alice back.

00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:00.610
That's right!

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:03.480
I create new entanglements.

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:04.400
Karen!

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:05.570
Karen?

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:07.820
There are two of you?

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:09.320
What's going on?

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:13.030
I don't understand.

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:14.950
What are you doing here?

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:17.160
I'm the one with the questions!

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:22.290
You said that assuming Yakumo's
identity and connecting to Arahabaki

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:25.880
was the only way to save Alice.

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:28.630
That <i>is </i>the only way.

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:30.390
Travel through time.

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:33.390
There are records of every attempt.

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:37.980
They are stored on Arahabaki,
and they prove that.

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:40.770
Then why can't I travel back 2,000 years?

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:41.940
What did you say?

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:44.480
Why have I failed at time travel?

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:46.400
Answer me!

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:49.900
Did I not help you?

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:51.610
It was you.

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:53.320
Huh?

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:59.120
Tell me everything you know, now!

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:05.500
Your entire memory will be mine!

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:34.280
He absorbed his memories?!

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:40.830
I see.

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:46.000
So this is what it's like to be
connected to Arahabaki.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:50.090
All its memories are now mine.

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:51.010
What?!

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:52.130
It can't be.

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:54.760
You have all of Arahabaki's data now?

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:13.780
What the hell is this?

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:36.050
You know nothing.

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:37.760
Y-You son of a...

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:41.520
No matter what you do or how hard you try,

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:48.230
you will never be anything more than
an infinitesimal fraction of what I am.

00:08:56.870 --> 00:08:59.330
How many times has it been?

00:08:59.330 --> 00:09:04.460
How many times have I transferred
the same data to my countless iterations?

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:09.380
But still the future does not change.

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:12.300
Alice cannot be saved.

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:17.390
I alone have observed
every single attempt.

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:19.100
I am the only one.

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:26.100
You, too, have struggled in vain,
and it has all come to nothing.

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:31.230
Don't flatter yourself. You're but
one individual amid the infinite.

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:33.070
Enough.

00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:34.320
Shut your mouth!

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:37.030
I don't wanna hear anymore!

00:09:37.030 --> 00:09:39.660
I <i>will </i>save her!

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:44.450
I don't care how many times it takes.
I <i>will </i>save Alice.

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:48.790
Damn you! Give me the Red Strings now!

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:59.970
Your attempt at time travel failed
because you didn't copy Yuito's power.

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:05.430
You can't sustain the Red Strings,
even with your own power?

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:07.140
So you keep copying it?

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:09.560
Resistance is futile.

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:13.070
I must have the Red Strings!

00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:14.110
Karen!

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:17.070
The world will be destroyed
if you time travel!

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:18.910
So what if it is?!

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:23.540
I <i>will </i>travel back in time again,
no matter what it takes!

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:25.750
Karen.

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:29.170
So you've no intention of helping us.

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:30.830
Please, listen!

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:33.670
New Himuka, the moon...

00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:35.710
The problems we face are endless,

00:10:35.710 --> 00:10:38.590
but we won't solve
anything if the world ends.

00:10:38.590 --> 00:10:41.340
We must forge a new future!

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:45.140
A world with such a dark history
isn't worth saving.

00:10:45.140 --> 00:10:50.190
I <i>will </i>change the past.
This time, I <i>will </i>succeed!

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:53.570
I understand that you want
to save Alice, but--

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:57.690
I don't need you to understand!
As if you even could!

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:05.330
His power is amplifying!

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:26.600
Yuito.

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:41.700
I ask you, could you give up on what
you treasure most in this world?!

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:46.620
After all manner of intensive training,

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:53.290
two young recruits have become
Scarlet Guardians, saviors of our planet.

00:11:55.090 --> 00:11:56.540
Nagi.

00:11:56.540 --> 00:11:59.630
They are Private First Class
Yuito Sumeragi

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:02.300
and Private First Class Nagi Karman.

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:07.720
Morning. It's supposed
to be a nice day today.

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:09.270
Sis.

00:12:11.270 --> 00:12:13.350
What could possibly go wrong?

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:18.730
Plus, you've wanted to join the OSF
ever since you were a kid.

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:25.740
How about we go out?

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:27.910
I've somewhere in mind.

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:31.040
Nagi!

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:32.960
Hey, Yuito.

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:34.620
Hey, Kasane.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:36.170
I know you want to.

00:12:36.170 --> 00:12:39.880
You care about me, right?
You'll return to the past and...

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:41.920
You want to help me, don't you?

00:13:02.650 --> 00:13:04.200
Kasane, I know you can...

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:08.160
Yuito, I know you can help me.

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:12.160
I know you regret it, don't you, Kasane?

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:15.580
If at that fateful moment,

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:18.710
you had noticed something was wrong,

00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:20.460
I wouldn't...

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:21.960
I wouldn't have...

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:28.680
I wouldn't have turned into this!

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:31.260
I know you regret it.

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:34.350
If at that fateful moment...

00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:36.270
What about Nagi?

00:13:36.270 --> 00:13:39.520
I haven't heard from him
since he was hospitalized.

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:44.320
This wouldn't have happened
if you had come found me.

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:48.280
I don't know what's going on anymore.

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:51.450
A voice is telling me to kill you.

00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:53.240
The voice...

00:13:53.240 --> 00:13:56.710
...it tells me to fight
even though I don't want to.

00:13:56.710 --> 00:13:59.880
I'm scared, but I can't defy it.

00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:02.460
I do have regrets.

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:05.220
If I'd made slightly different choices,

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:09.260
the future might have been
completely different.

00:14:09.260 --> 00:14:10.390
But...

00:14:10.390 --> 00:14:14.470
You always have to make
one choice over another.

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:18.060
As long as you draw breath,
you make your choice and move forward.

00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:19.810
That's all we can do.

00:14:19.810 --> 00:14:23.270
We must choose what we believe
is right at that moment.

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:39.210
In the end, you had it your own way.

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:41.750
You abandoned the one you care for.

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:44.500
That is the extent of your caring.

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:47.800
N-No! Nagi was there for me, so--

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:49.760
Don't you pretend to understand!

00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:52.140
Nagi was there for me!

00:14:52.140 --> 00:14:57.350
I must not turn my eyes from anything,
including what happened to Nagi.

00:14:57.350 --> 00:14:59.640
That's what I've come to believe!

00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:03.690
We must face the future
without trying to change the past.

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:05.530
That's what we must do.

00:15:05.530 --> 00:15:07.740
Those are just excuses!

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:09.280
You're giving up on the past.

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:12.370
You're averting your eyes
and running from tragedy.

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:16.200
But I won't run! I'll do
whatever it takes to save Alice!

00:15:16.200 --> 00:15:17.700
Karen! Please, listen!

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:23.080
You must have a memory of Alice
that made you want to move forward.

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:24.250
What?!

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:26.000
Think about it!

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:30.180
Would Alice really want to be saved
if it meant the end of the world?

00:15:30.180 --> 00:15:32.260
Don't you dare talk about Alice!

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:36.850
I know you must understand now!
You connected to Arahabaki, after all!

00:15:36.850 --> 00:15:38.480
You must know how Alice feels!

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:42.980
Enough! Nothing I could ever
learn would change my mind,

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:45.650
no matter how far the world
plunges into chaos!

00:15:51.490 --> 00:15:54.280
I won't change my mind!

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:57.580
I won't...!

00:15:57.580 --> 00:15:59.370
Give it to me, now!

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:03.540
I want your Red Strings!

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:06.380
Kasane! It's time!

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:11.930
I'll have no more use for you
once I have the Red Strings!

00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:14.970
Kasane! Let's fight fire with fire!

00:16:14.970 --> 00:16:16.430
What?!

00:16:19.770 --> 00:16:20.980
Huh?!

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:46.880
Let's scour Arahabaki's memory to find
the truth behind who Alice really is!

00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:49.130
She was a lovely person.

00:16:49.130 --> 00:16:53.510
Your intense desire
to save her proves that.

00:17:00.850 --> 00:17:02.640
Alice?

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:04.600
Thanks.

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:06.860
What's the matter?

00:17:06.860 --> 00:17:09.480
It's Karen.

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:12.900
You know how he's always
coming to my rescue.

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:16.530
But today, Karen was
wounded because of me.

00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:19.870
That was more than a scratch.

00:17:19.870 --> 00:17:22.750
That's just how he is.

00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:26.370
I never asked Karen to save me.

00:17:26.370 --> 00:17:31.420
I just wish he would care
more about himself.

00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:33.050
Me, too.

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:49.810
I never want to lose him.

00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:52.860
I'll have to get my act together.

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:55.360
Even then...

00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:58.490
...I bet he'd still look out for you.

00:17:58.490 --> 00:17:59.950
You're right.

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:05.250
That's all the more reason
why I have to do better.

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:17.260
I must work harder to make sure Karen
is not always worrying about me.

00:18:19.300 --> 00:18:23.350
I want him to be happy.

00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:28.650
Karen Travers...

00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:30.940
How do you feel now?

00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:33.020
Are you happy?

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:49.790
Alice.

00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:12.190
Is it over?

00:19:12.190 --> 00:19:14.440
I think so.

00:19:14.440 --> 00:19:15.570
I...

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:18.360
I...

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:23.950
I cannot accept this!

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:30.040
There is no way I can ever accept this!

00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:31.210
Karen!

00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:44.680
Yuito!

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:55.730
Now I have copied your Red Strings.

00:19:55.730 --> 00:19:58.650
This time, I will not fail!

00:20:04.370 --> 00:20:07.990
Karen, you saw it with your own eyes.

00:20:07.990 --> 00:20:11.120
You saw how Alice really feels.

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:15.000
Alice, I'm coming for you.

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:17.090
I <i>will </i>save you.

00:20:24.430 --> 00:20:27.560
I will never stop.

00:20:27.560 --> 00:20:30.390
This time, it will be different.

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:33.520
I won't fail to save Alice.

00:20:34.850 --> 00:20:36.650
My brother is too far gone.

00:20:53.960 --> 00:20:54.920
Yuito.

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:57.500
Yeah, he's forced our hand!

00:21:34.330 --> 00:21:35.670
Karen!

00:22:34.060 --> 00:22:41.900
<i>I've been a prisoner</i>
<i>of my own longing</i>

00:22:43.690 --> 00:22:51.490
<i>The shimmering heat signals me to halt</i>

00:22:51.490 --> 00:22:53.620
<i>There's a stranger in me</i>

00:22:53.620 --> 00:22:56.120
<i>I'll fly high so I won't be scared</i>

00:22:56.120 --> 00:23:01.380
<i>By this new self I've never seen</i>

00:23:01.380 --> 00:23:03.170
<i>I'm spreading my wings</i>

00:23:03.170 --> 00:23:05.510
<i>Bird in florid flight</i>

00:23:05.510 --> 00:23:10.220
<i>Lift your eyes to the scarlet sky</i>

00:23:10.220 --> 00:23:15.430
<i>Overtaken by the mighty wind</i>

00:23:15.430 --> 00:23:20.600
<i>The view unfolds upon a world</i>
<i>that begins turning</i>

00:23:20.600 --> 00:23:25.070
<i>Amid the intermingling light</i>

00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:30.950
<i>I keep searching for tomorrow</i>

00:23:30.950 --> 00:23:32.570
<i>Tomorrow's in your hands</i>

00:23:32.570 --> 00:23:35.790
<i>Don't tell me now you're afraid</i>

00:23:35.790 --> 00:23:37.410
<i>There's no time to waste</i>

00:23:37.410 --> 00:23:40.370
<i>Keep going forward</i>

00:23:40.370 --> 00:23:44.710
<i>There's nothing to be afraid of</i>

00:23:44.710 --> 00:23:46.380
<i>Now, let's go</i>

00:23:46.380 --> 00:23:51.840
<i>Into a brand-new day</i>

00:24:09.150 --> 00:24:11.950
"Operation Destroy the Kunad Gate"
